From: PwndaWallet <pwndamining@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 10/12] redeem: treat an already-mined coin-A spend as success,
 not a fatal action failure

A completed atomic swap can present as a permanently failed one.

`redeemXmrBidCoinALockTx` (the follower's chain-A redeem) calls `publishTx`
bare. `checkQueuedActions` drives it from a periodic tick, and the bookkeeping
that records the redeem -- `bid.xmr_a_lock_spend_tx`, written at the END of
that function -- only lands after the publish returns. An interruption between
the two (a wallet re-lock, a restart, a dropped RPC session) leaves a redeem
that is genuinely confirmed on-chain and a bid that has no record of it.

The next tick rebuilds the same deterministic transaction and rebroadcasts it.
The chain correctly rejects the duplicate. Upstream treats that rejection as a
fatal action failure and parks the bid in `BID_ERROR` -- and `checkXmrBidState`
has no `BID_ERROR` branch, unlike its non-XMR sibling `checkBidState`, which
carries an explicit `pass  # Wait for user input`. So the bid stops being
tracked, while the funds it is tracking already arrived.

Observed on mainnet XMR->LTC, 2026-08-23, verbatim:

    checkQueuedActions failed: Electrum error: {'code': 1, 'message': 'the
    transaction was rejected by network rules.\n\nTransaction already in block
    chain\n'}

Two independent defects, both fixed here:

1. `isTxExistsError`'s electrum branch matched only "Transaction outputs
   already in utxo set" -- the UNCONFIRMED / mempool-collision message. The
   CONFIRMED case, which is the one this predicate exists to catch, arrives as
   "Transaction already in block chain" (the exact wording the non-electrum
   branch already matched). So on an electrum-mode wallet the predicate
   answered False for its own primary case.

2. The redeem path never called it at all. The coin-A *refund* path is the
   only caller in the tree; the redeem path -- equally deterministic, equally
   re-attemptable -- had no equivalent handling.

The fix mirrors the refund path exactly: recover the txid locally via
`getTxid` and fall through to the same bookkeeping, so an already-successful
redeem is recorded rather than retried forever. Deliberately narrow -- every
other publish failure still raises, because only "this exact transaction is
already on chain" is safe to read as success.

Upstream-PR candidate: this is a correctness bug in upstream's own code, not
embedder policy. Any BasicSwap user on an electrum-mode BTC/LTC wallet can hit
it, and both halves are wrong independent of how the node is embedded.

Marker: PWNDA-PATCH-10
---
--- a/basicswap/interface/btc/btc.py
+++ b/basicswap/interface/btc/btc.py
@@ -4949,8 +4949,25 @@
         return None
 
     def isTxExistsError(self, err_str: str) -> bool:
+        # PWNDA-PATCH-10: the electrum branch missed the message electrum
+        # actually returns for an already-MINED transaction.
+        #
+        # ElectrumX relays the node's own rejection verbatim, so a duplicate
+        # broadcast of a CONFIRMED transaction arrives as:
+        #     the transaction was rejected by network rules.
+        #     Transaction already in block chain
+        # which is the same "already in block chain" wording the non-electrum
+        # branch below already matches. "Transaction outputs already in utxo
+        # set" is a real electrum message too, but it is the UNCONFIRMED /
+        # mempool-collision case -- so matching only that one made this
+        # predicate answer False for the confirmed case it exists to catch,
+        # and every caller relying on it fell through to a fatal error.
+        # Observed on mainnet LTC 2026-08-23. Both messages are accepted now.
         if self._connection_type == "electrum":
-            return "Transaction outputs already in utxo set" in err_str
+            return (
+                "Transaction outputs already in utxo set" in err_str
+                or "Transaction already in block chain" in err_str
+            )
         return "Transaction already in block chain" in err_str
 
     def isTxNonFinalError(self, err_str: str) -> bool:
--- a/basicswap/basicswap.py
+++ b/basicswap/basicswap.py
@@ -13007,7 +13007,39 @@
             xmr_swap.a_lock_spend_tx = tx.serialize_without_witness()
             xmr_swap.a_lock_spend_tx_id = ci_from.getTxid(xmr_swap.a_lock_spend_tx)
 
-        txid = bytes.fromhex(ci_from.publishTx(xmr_swap.a_lock_spend_tx))
+        # PWNDA-PATCH-10: a duplicate broadcast of an already-mined redeem is
+        # a SUCCESS, not a failure.
+        #
+        # Upstream calls publishTx bare here. checkQueuedActions runs this on
+        # a periodic tick, and the bookkeeping that records the redeem
+        # (bid.xmr_a_lock_spend_tx, saved at the end of this function) only
+        # lands after the publish returns -- so an interruption between the
+        # two leaves a redeem that is genuinely on-chain and a bid that does
+        # not know it. The next tick rebuilds the SAME deterministic tx,
+        # rebroadcasts it, and the chain correctly rejects the duplicate.
+        # Upstream treats that rejection as a fatal action failure and parks
+        # the bid in BID_ERROR -- which checkXmrBidState has no branch to
+        # resume from -- so a swap that actually COMPLETED presents as "needs
+        # attention" indefinitely. Observed on mainnet XMR->LTC 2026-08-23.
+        #
+        # The coin-A refund path already handles this exact case with
+        # isTxExistsError; the redeem path simply never did. Mirror it:
+        # recover the txid locally and fall through to the SAME bookkeeping,
+        # so an already-successful redeem is recorded instead of retried
+        # forever. Deliberately narrow -- any other publish failure still
+        # raises, because only "this exact tx is already on chain" is safe to
+        # read as success.
+        try:
+            txid = bytes.fromhex(ci_from.publishTx(xmr_swap.a_lock_spend_tx))
+        except Exception as ex:
+            if not ci_from.isTxExistsError(str(ex)):
+                raise
+            txid = ci_from.getTxid(xmr_swap.a_lock_spend_tx)
+            self.log.info(
+                f"PWNDA-PATCH-10: coin A lock spend tx for bid "
+                f"{self.log.id(bid_id)} is already on chain "
+                f"({self.logIDT(txid)}); recording it rather than failing."
+            )
         self.log.debug(
             f"Submitted lock spend txn {self.logIDT(txid)} to {ci_from.coin_name()} chain for bid {self.log.id(bid_id)}."
         )
